% under simultaneous application of a reference input and a disturbance
% input is then as follows.
%
% $$ \dot{\Theta}_{m}(s) = \frac{K_eK_m(K_ps+K_i)}{\tau s^2+(1+K_eK_mK_p)s +
% K_eK_mK_i}\dot{\Theta}_{ref}(s) + \frac{K_m s}{\tau
% s^2+(1+K_eK_mK_p)s+K_eK_mK_i}T_L(s) $$
%
% For the purposes of this activity, we will simply examine the
% steady-state error that the closed-loop system will experience under the
% influence of an approximately constant disturbance load torque. To
% predict the kind of behavior we expect, we can apply the final value
% theorem. 
%
% $$ \dot{\theta}_{m,ss} = \lim_{t \rightarrow \infty} \dot{\theta}_m(t) =
% \lim_{s \rightarrow 0} s\dot{\Theta}_m(s) = \lim_{s \rightarrow 0} s
